# Redoubt gradle-no-config-cache.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M3-13 ("The Gradle configuration cache breaks the Kotlin build")
#
# THE FAULT
# ---------
# Every multi-ABI Gecko/AAR build died at :geckoview:compileDebugKotlin with:
#
#   > Could not load the value of field `__buildFusService__` of task
#     `:geckoview:compileDebugKotlin` of type
#     `org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.tasks.KotlinCompile`.
#   >   > Cannot set the value of a property of type
#       org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.plugin.statistics.BuildFusService using a
#       provider of type
#       org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.plugin.statistics.FlowActionBuildFusService.
#
# The operative word is LOAD. This is configuration-cache DESERIALIZATION, not
# service registration: KGP writes the FUS (usage-statistics) build service
# into the configuration cache as FlowActionBuildFusService and reads it back
# into a field declared BuildFusService. The types do not round-trip.
#
# WHAT IT COST, AND THE THREE WRONG DIAGNOSES IT PRODUCED
# --------------------------------------------------------
# The fault presents as intermittent and target-specific, and it is neither.
# Recorded here because the same shape will recur:
#
#   1. "It is ARM-specific."  Both ARM ABIs failed and x86_64 appeared to pass.
#      The x86_64 "pass" was a 2026-08-22 run; re-running x86_64 on 2026-08-24
#      failed identically. The ABI was never the variable.
#   2. "It is a Kotlin version mismatch."  gradle/libs.versions.toml pins
#      kotlin 2.3.21 while Gradle 9.5.1 embeds kotlin-dsl 2.3.20, and the build
#      log itself flags this as "not recommended". Aligning 2.3.21 -> 2.3.20
#      did not fix it; the fault reproduced on all three ABIs at 2.3.20. The
#      mismatch is real and harmless.
#   3. "It is a stale configuration cache."  Deleting
#      <srcdir>/.gradle/configuration-cache did not fix it either. The cache is
#      not stale, it is unusable: a freshly written entry fails to load.
#
# Note for anyone tempted to chase it with a fresh --outdir: the configuration
# cache lives in the SOURCE tree at <srcdir>/.gradle/configuration-cache, not
# in the output directory, so a new outdir does not clear it and never did.
#
# THE FIX
# -------
# Turn the configuration cache off for the Android build. Measured 2026-08-24:
# with org.gradle.configuration-cache=false, :geckoview:compileDebugKotlin
# completes and the build proceeds into the Rust compile stage, at the same
# Kotlin 2.3.21 that upstream pins.
#
# The cost is small here and the benefit is not: the configuration cache speeds
# up the CONFIGURATION phase of repeated builds. Redoubt's Gecko/AAR builds are
# from-scratch release builds in a container, where configuration is a rounding
# error against a ~20 minute Rust and C++ compile. We trade a few seconds of
# configuration time for a build that completes.
#
# Revisit when the Kotlin Gradle plugin fixes the round-trip. The check is one
# line: flip this to true and run a single ABI pass.
--- a/gradle.properties
+++ b/gradle.properties
@@ -10,6 +10,6 @@
 # Do not modify these values without first reviewing Bug 1954747: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1954747
 org.gradle.jvmargs=-Xmx7g -Xms2g -XX:MaxMetaspaceSize=6g -XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError -XX:+UseParallelGC
 
-org.gradle.configuration-cache=true
+org.gradle.configuration-cache=false
 
 android.useAndroidX=true
